#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305311 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d54af84f-cbbc-5372-ba07-e261c20bd3c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{31}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305313} {:answer/id #uuid "df41c6c3-3a00-5138-8a93-244385e7d4dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305314} {:answer/id #uuid "8873aec4-e1a0-5c4f-97c2-ae8dd35eec80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{31}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305315} {:answer/id #uuid "56620c1c-6328-51a8-86fd-15180501d1cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{62}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305316} {:answer/id #uuid "bdb6d05f-4105-5261-999b-ba078ba6350f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdb6d05f-4105-5261-999b-ba078ba6350f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305317} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e619283-44d5-5221-8403-3681fc222179" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e0ae544d-cc6c-5242-be1f-c4ab12022dac" :question/math-academy-id "q-127866" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,ABC,$ if $A(5,0,5),$ $B(6,-1,4),$ $C(9,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(6i-j+4k)-(5i+5k) \\\\  & =i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(9i+j)-(5i+5k) \\\\  & =4i+j-5k \\\\  & =⟨4,1,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-5)-1\\cdot (-1))i-(1\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot (-1))j+(1\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =6i+j+5k \\\\  & =⟨6,1,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{62}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324594 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "204ec977-b1ba-5c6f-9231-575c58f156dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324596} {:answer/id #uuid "756736f5-f53e-5f2e-845c-b194756d5650" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324597} {:answer/id #uuid "2f78357d-0ab4-5517-ad10-1ff518f19027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324598} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba431f3-3db3-5f36-905b-50991616823b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324599} {:answer/id #uuid "0b628283-4da3-5123-b0f0-2a6ba0715389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "204ec977-b1ba-5c6f-9231-575c58f156dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324596} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb2eddcf-f48f-5705-a434-dcc471f726e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "588b7ac8-1d13-58bf-8be3-40e1395c4ae0" :question/math-academy-id "q-127915" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,WXY,$ if $W(3,9,4),$ $X(1,7,3),$ $Y(6,12,8).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX} & =x-w \\\\  & =(i+7j+3k)-(3i+9j+4k) \\\\  & =-2i-2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =y-w \\\\  & =(6i+12j+8k)-(3i+9j+4k) \\\\  & =3i+3j+4k \\\\  & =⟨3,3,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot (-1))i-((-2)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot (-1))j+((-2)\\cdot 3-3\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-5i+5j \\\\  & =⟨-5,5,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+{5}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,WXY$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305353 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9331987e-8676-5bdb-b4ce-2129b1b09a8c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Altitude of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1253243a-eac3-5cb7-9453-0078bf32091b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305355} {:answer/id #uuid "55a9cdc3-3833-56f4-a3da-dd76e13921e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55a9cdc3-3833-56f4-a3da-dd76e13921e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305356} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c1bcbd9-c2a5-50d2-bfad-900ea89dec66" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "370d2d9d-9da0-5ac7-82a8-fa08d76b3133" :question/math-academy-id "q-275225" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(-2,0,-1)$, $B(0,-2,-1)$, $C(-3,-2,0).$\n\n$CH=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2j-k)-(-2i-k) \\\\  & =2i-2j \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-3i-2j)-(-2i-k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 0)i-(2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)j+(2\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-2i-2j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{44} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{11}}{2}=\\sqrt{11}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ \\sqrt{11} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{11} & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9331987e-8676-5bdb-b4ce-2129b1b09a8c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Altitude of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15ea403b-a3b7-5823-805c-83dd5f0a467e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315842} {:answer/id #uuid "549549a3-b5e7-56df-b0f0-96ad058949be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{38}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15ea403b-a3b7-5823-805c-83dd5f0a467e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315842} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9028da6-1499-5ed9-92f0-b5c25697381f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1e929d09-28f2-5088-a9e8-afcb5cdf64da" :question/math-academy-id "q-316409" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $IP$ of the $△\\,HIJ$, if $H(-1,2,0)$, $I(1,1,3)$, $J(0,-2,1).$\n\n$IP=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $IP$ can be related to the area of $△\\,HIJ$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}IP\\cdot HJ\n$$\n\nSo, to find $IP,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{HI}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HJ} & =j-h \\\\  & =(-2j+k)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =i-4j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,-4,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{HI} & =i-h \\\\  & =(i+j+3k)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =2i-j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HJ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{HI} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))i-(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2)j+(1\\cdot (-1)-(-4)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-11i-j+7k \\\\  & =⟨-11,-1,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{HI}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{HJ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{HI}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-11)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{171} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,HIJ$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{19}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $HJ$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}HJ & =|\\overset{\\to }{HJ}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}IP\\cdot HJ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}IP\\cdot HJ \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{19}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,IP\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{19} & =\\sqrt{2}\\,IP \\\\ IP & =\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305367 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "875f8dcb-5039-5964-ba26-3f56de0ce03a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305369} {:answer/id #uuid "ec7e58ae-973a-546c-83e8-dd818521ee60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "875f8dcb-5039-5964-ba26-3f56de0ce03a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305369} :answer-field/id #uuid "851d5934-360b-5f83-a502-7978cec33428" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ffc323ce-db7c-5144-9dd9-04891b843444" :question/math-academy-id "q-316530" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,STU,$ if $S(0,1,2),$ $T(2,3,1),$ $U(4,1,2).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{ST}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SU}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ST} & =t-s \\\\  & =(2i+3j+k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{SU} & =u-s \\\\  & =(4i+j+2k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =4i+0j+0k \\\\  & =⟨4,0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ST}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SU} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 0)i-(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 4)j+(2\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =0i-4j-8k \\\\  & =⟨0,-4,-8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{ST}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SU}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{ST}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SU}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,STU$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{2}=2\\sqrt{5}.\n$$"}]}
